;; bin/pyi runtime check's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a); queue 235): per family a crossed pair, the
;; subject's run by pyi judged by the check's own judge (the outcome's text equal: stdout, "status N" and stderr's last line
;; for a program, smoke_run; stdout, the status and the whole stderr for a REPL session, repl_run) against the reference's
;; outcome by the oracle (test/python/records/outcomes/, or python3 where it runs live), which must differ. Both files pass
;; in the check. "control passed:" or "control not judged:" fails the check (bin/pyi smoke_controls); the subjects run with
;; every PYI_SMOKE_ONLY selection. No control is a program or session of the counts. Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "smoke-1" :family :smoke :subject "arith.py" :reference "calls.py"
  :why "two of the first smoke programs (7 and 29 lines): arithmetic's printed results against calls' (other stdout, both status 0)"}
 {:id "repl-1" :family :repl :subject "e-repl-b.in" :reference "e-repl.in"
  :why "a three-statement session against the REPL's 30-line session (other prompts and values; e-repl.in's exit status 2, e-repl-b.in's 0)"}]
